# Contract-major 2 inclusive ranges

[Run the 1.0.0 release walkthrough in Livebook](https://livebook.dev/run?url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fbaselabs%2Fbounded_authority_protocol%2Fblob%2Fv1.0.0%2Fdocs%2Flivebooks%2Fbap-walkthrough.livemd).
For this focused journey, download this `.livemd` file and use **Open → Import from file**.
This file is new since 1.0.0; the released walkthrough does not exercise contract-major 2 ranges.

Integer and float tags are distinct even when their numeric values coincide. Each refusal
below has a freshly signed proof matching the supplied arguments, so the selector is what fails.

```elixir
Mix.install([{:bounded_authority_protocol, "== 1.0.0"}])
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
:ok
```

## Build a bounded contract-major 2 grant

```elixir
alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V2
alias BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.{Credentials, ExpectedRequest, TrustedIssuer}
{issuer_public, issuer_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:eddsa, :ed25519)
{holder_public, holder_private} = :crypto.generate_key(:eddsa, :ed25519)
{:ok, thumbprint} = BoundedAuthorityProtocol.V1.Jwk.public_key_thumbprint_raw(holder_public, %{})
now = 1_800_000_100
sign = fn input, key ->
  signature = :crypto.sign(:eddsa, :none, input.message, [key, :ed25519])
  {:ok, compact} = V2.assemble_compact(input, signature)
  compact
end
grant = %V2.Grant{
  key_id: "issuer-1", issuer: "https://issuer.example", grant_id: "range-1",
  audiences: ["https://compute.example"], issued_at: now, not_before: now,
  expires_at: now + 3_600, holder_thumbprint: thumbprint,
  operations: [%V2.Operation{name: "allocate_workers", selectors: [
    {:gte, ["workers"], {:integer, 1}}, {:lte, ["workers"], {:integer, 8}}
  ]}]
}
{:ok, input} = V2.grant_signing_input(grant, %{})
compact = sign.(input, issuer_private)
true = is_binary(compact)
:range_grant_assembled
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
:range_grant_assembled
```

## Inclusive boundaries and tag mismatch

```elixir
check = fn tagged ->
  arguments = {:object, [{"workers", tagged}]}
  proof = %V2.Proof{
    holder_public_key: holder_public, proof_id: "range-proof", method: "POST",
    target_uri: "https://compute.example/jobs", issued_at: now, nonce: nil,
    invocation_id: "7d444840-9dc0-11ed-a8fc-0242ac120002", operation: "allocate_workers",
    grant_compact: compact, cast_arguments: arguments
  }
  {:ok, proof_input} = V2.proof_signing_input(proof, %{})
  credentials = %Credentials{grant: compact, proof: sign.(proof_input, holder_private)}
  expected = %ExpectedRequest{
    trusted_issuer: %TrustedIssuer{key_id: "issuer-1", public_key: issuer_public},
    issuer: "https://issuer.example", audience: "https://compute.example", method: "POST",
    target_uri: proof.target_uri, invocation_id: proof.invocation_id, operation: proof.operation,
    cast_arguments: arguments, evaluation_time: now, clock_skew: 0,
    proof_max_age: 300, nonce: :not_required, bounds: %{}
  }
  case V2.check_envelope(credentials, expected) do
    {:ok, facts} -> {:ok, facts.authorization}
    error -> error
  end
end
results = Enum.map([{:integer, 1}, {:integer, 8}, {:integer, 0}, {:integer, 9}, {:float, 1.0}], check)
[{:ok, :not_evaluated}, {:ok, :not_evaluated}, {:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}] = results
results
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
[{:ok, :not_evaluated}, {:ok, :not_evaluated}, {:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}]
```

## Invalid selectors never produce signing bytes

```elixir
results = for selector <- [{:lte, ["workers"], {:string, "8"}}, {:gte, [], {:integer, 1}}] do
  operation = %V2.Operation{name: "allocate_workers", selectors: [selector]}
  V2.grant_signing_input(%{grant | operations: [operation]}, %{})
end
[{:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}] = results
results
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
[{:error, :invalid}, {:error, :invalid}]
```
